en.math:
\begin{aligned}
    4\pi r^2 A_r
    &=
    -4\pi G M_{\mathrm{enc}}(r),\\
    &\boxed{
      A_r(r)
      =
      -\frac{G M_{\mathrm{enc}}(r)}{r^2}.}
  \end{aligned}

p.src:
Multiplying the acceleration by a test mass $m$ gives $m\ddot r
  =
  -m\frac{4\pi G\rho}{3}r.$ This is a harmonic oscillator with $\omega^2=\frac{4\pi G\rho}{3}
  =\frac{GM}{R^3}
  =\frac{g_{\mathrm s}}{R},$ where $g_{\mathrm s}=GM/R^2$ is the surface acceleration. A frictionless tunnel through the idealized uniform Earth would therefore produce an oscillation through the center and back.

