p.src:
Take a ray that just skims the Sun, whose mass and radius are $M$ and $R$. Near closest approach, approximate the downward acceleration by the surface value $g_\odot\approx\frac{GM}{R^2}.$ The ray spends roughly one solar diameter in the strong-field region, so $\Delta t\approx\frac{2R}{c}.$ Its acquired transverse velocity is then $\Delta v_\perp
  \approx
  g_\odot\Delta t
  \approx
  \frac{2GM}{Rc}.$ For a small angle, $\boxed{
  \theta_{\mathrm{Newton}}
  \approx
  \frac{\Delta v_\perp}{c}
  \approx
  \frac{2GM}{Rc^2}.}$

